+    <article class="method-card"><span class="eyebrow">01 / SCIENTIFIC EVIDENCE</span><h3>Sources you can trace.</h3><p>TerraTrend automatically discovers monthly NASA MERRA-2 observations through CMR and downloads native-grid subsets from GES DISC, the archive behind the challenge’s Giovanni resource. Each result retains the dataset citation, units, native cell spacing, coverage and geographic boundary version.</p><div class="resource-links"><a href="https://giovanni.gsfc.nasa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Giovanni ↗</a><a href="https://disc.gsfc.nasa.gov/information/tools?title=Hydrology%20Time%20Series" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hydrology Time Series ↗</a><a href="https://appeears.earthdatacloud.nasa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AppEEARS ↗</a><a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/cdo-web/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Climate Data Online ↗</a><a href="https://climexp.knmi.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KNMI Climate Explorer ↗</a></div><p class="micro">The existing NASA POWER cache is available for continuity and is labeled separately. Its access route has not been verified against this resource list. No new POWER downloads are made by the map workflow.</p></article>
+    <article class="method-card"><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE MEASUREMENT</span><h3>Whole areas. Honest coverage.</h3><p>Native grid cells are clipped to the chosen boundary and weighted by their overlap and latitude. At least 80% area support and complete calendar years are required. Small regions can share a coarse source cell: a sharp boundary does not add scientific resolution.</p><p>Theil–Sen measures the trend; Mann–Kendall tests significance. Monthly seasonality, confidence intervals and autocorrelation checks are available in Analysis. Paired calendar-aligned series support A/B comparisons.</p><p class="micro">Remote links represent statistical associations and possible lead relationships, not established physical causes or measured wind trajectories. Anomaly relationships do not by themselves explain a long-term trend.</p></article>
+    <article class="method-card"><span class="eyebrow">03 / GEOGRAPHIC REFERENCE</span><h3>One boundary, every view.</h3><p>Global country boundaries use Natural Earth 1:50m, including the disconnected parts present at that resolution. Continental and subcontinental layers follow UN country membership; transcontinental countries remain whole in this scheme.</p><p>All 16 Ghana regions are bundled. Other countries load first-level administrative boundaries on demand through geoBoundaries gbOpen when available. Reference boundaries are separate from scientific measurements.</p><a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Natural Earth · public domain ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/virgoaugustine/Ghana-GeoJSON-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ghana boundary attribution ↗</a><a href="https://www.geoboundaries.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">geoBoundaries ↗</a></article>
+    <article class="method-card automatic-source-card"><span class="eyebrow">04 / AUTOMATIC NASA DATA</span><h3>Connect once. Analyze anywhere.</h3><p>Choose an area and period, then Analyze. TerraTrend fetches the published monthly grids, clips them to your actual boundary and caches them for reuse. No file uploads are needed.</p><p id="earthdata-status" class="connection-status" role="status">Checking the NASA connection…</p>
+      <div id="nasa-restart-help" class="nasa-restart-help" hidden><strong>Start the updated server</strong><ol><li>In the terminal running TerraTrend, press Ctrl+C.</li><li>From the project folder, run <code>./start.sh 8517</code>.</li><li>Reload this page, then connect Earthdata below.</li></ol><p class="micro">Your selected areas stay prepared while you view these instructions. A page reload starts a new investigation.</p></div>
+      <form id="earthdata-connect-form"><label for="earthdata-token">EARTHDATA USER TOKEN</label><input id="earthdata-token" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste your Earthdata-generated token" required minlength="20" maxlength="4096" disabled><p class="micro">Generate a user token in your <a href="https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA Earthdata profile ↗</a>. Approve GES DISC access if NASA requests it. The token stays in this server’s memory until restart and is sent only to NASA’s data service.</p><button class="hud-btn" type="submit" id="earthdata-connect" disabled>CONNECT EARTHDATA</button><button id="earthdata-disconnect" class="link-btn" type="button" hidden>DISCONNECT THIS SESSION</button></form>
+      <div class="automatic-coverage"><span class="eyebrow">VERIFIED AUTOMATIC MEASUREMENTS</span><p>Air temperature · Surface temperature · Specific humidity · Surface pressure · Root-zone soil moisture · Surface soil moisture · Land evaporation · Precipitation</p><p class="micro">Other catalogue variables still need verified source mappings. Monthly wind components cannot substitute for mean wind speed; solar radiation products cannot substitute for direct normal irradiance. Missing observations remain missing.</p></div><p class="micro">First downloads may take several minutes for large areas or long periods; progress and cancellation are available. Source granule IDs, collection version, observed dates and area coverage accompany each result.</p>
+    </article>
+    <article class="method-card import-card"><details><summary>Advanced · use an existing normalized dataset</summary><form id="resource-import-form">
+      <label>RESOURCE<select name="source" required><option value="giovanni">Giovanni</option><option value="hydrology">Hydrology Time Series</option><option value="appeears">AppEEARS</option><option value="cdo">Climate Data Online</option><option value="knmi">KNMI Climate Explorer</option></select></label>
+      <label>DATASET NAME<input name="name" placeholder="Dataset and collection version" required maxlength="150"></label>
+      <label>VARIABLE<select name="variable" id="import-variable" required></select></label>
+      <label>VALUES ARE IN<input name="unit" id="import-unit" required></label>
+      <div class="import-spacing"><label>CELL WIDTH (DEGREES)<input name="dlon" type="number" value="0.625" min="0.01" max="10" step="any" required></label><label>CELL HEIGHT (DEGREES)<input name="dlat" type="number" value="0.5" min="0.01" max="10" step="any" required></label></div>
+      <label>MISSING-DATA FILL VALUE (OPTIONAL)<input name="fill_value" type="number" step="any" placeholder="For example, -9999"></label>
+      <label>SOURCE CITATION / DATASET URL<textarea name="citation" required rows="2" placeholder="Where the observations came from, collection/version and export date"></textarea></label>
+      <label>MONTHLY GRID CSV<input name="file" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv" required></label>
+      <p class="micro">Required columns: <code>lon,lat,month,value</code>. One native-cell mean per YYYY-MM month. Convert units, apply the resource’s quality flags and aggregate daily exports before importing. Blank values and common NASA fill codes are excluded. Area-average CSVs cannot be used as spatial grids. Use the same dataset name and resource to associate additional variables from that collection.</p>
+      <button class="hud-btn" type="submit">IMPORT DATASET</button><p id="import-status" role="status" class="micro"></p>
+    </form></details></article>
+  </div>
+</section>
+<div class="map-bottom-bar"><div id="active-variable-strip" class="active-variable-strip" aria-label="Active map variable"></div><div class="map-color-key"><span><i class="rise-dot"></i>INCREASING</span><span><i class="fall-dot"></i>DECREASING</span><span><i class="neutral-dot"></i>NOT SIGNIFICANT</span><span><i class="missing-dot"></i>INSUFFICIENT DATA</span></div></div>
+<div id="work-progress" class="work-progress" role="status" hidden><span class="spin"></span><div><strong id="work-progress-title">Analyzing</strong><span id="work-progress-detail"></span></div><button id="cancel-work" type="button">CANCEL</button></div>
+
